   The article describes ways to generate asemic writing using
   \MetaPost, MetaFun, and LuaMetaFun\ in \ConTeXt. The term asemic
   means no semantic content and thus asemic writing is writing without
   semantic content or meaning. It has a thriving community of artists
   producing many different styles which can best be described as a
   hybrid form of abstract art. Examples of hand-written and \ConTeXt\
   generated asemic writing will be presented along with examples of the
   code used to produce them.
